  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nComputing $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =F(1) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.2 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $b,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =F(3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2,3}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =0.1+0.2+0.2+0.4 \\\\  & =0.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $c,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =F(4) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =0.1+0.2+0.2+0.4+0.1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.3+0.9+1=2.2.\n$$",
